  "repairs": [
    "Check complete native Job PID counts and returned byte length, bounded checked allocation growth, and a strict 1048576-ID ceiling at the prior nominal limit.",
    "Open noninheritable synchronization/query handles and affirm membership of that exact process object in the exact held Job before retaining it for a wait.",
    "Retain verified members before the owned Job termination request; a capture failure or expiry cannot suppress that request for active or unknown work.",
    "Use one absolute five-second confirmation deadline from before the initial query through capture, retained WaitAll batches, final Job accounting, and the original-child wait. Compute the original-child wait allowance at its actual boundary.",
    "Preserve actual native results and errors; overdue, failed, missing or incomplete required proof vetoes success even if the Job later empties.",
    "Release retained member handles on every return path and before final Job accounting. Restrict the old unused unsorted query wrapper to tests; leave the live sorted extension helper unchanged."
  ],
